    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98-a3">

                <pb facs="0227" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg187"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure No. 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Kirkpatrick to Governor Rawson.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate</hi>. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Nassau,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 31, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to ask your excellency’s
                    permission for the United States ship-of-war Honduras, Captain Harris, to anchor
                    in the harbor to transact some business with this consulate in regard to payment
                    of salvage to the wreckers of the United States ship San Jacinto, lately
                    wrecked.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS KIRKPATRICK</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rawso. W. Rawson</hi>. C. B., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Governor of Bahamas.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
